## Memory Optimization: Shared Local Memory (SLM) Tiling

### Objective
Reduce global memory traffic by caching frequently reused data in fast on-chip shared local memory (SLM). This is essential when data is accessed multiple times by different work-items within a work-group.

### Required Transformations

**1. Allocate and Load Tiles into SLM**
Use collaborative loading where each work-item loads one or more elements:

```cpp
constexpr int TILE_SIZE = 16;  // Choose based on SLM capacity (typically 64KB total)

// Allocate local memory tile (one per work-group, shared by all work-items)
auto tile = sycl::ext::oneapi::group_local_memory_for_overwrite<float[TILE_SIZE][TILE_SIZE]>(item.get_group());

// Get local and global indices
int local_row = item.get_local_id(0);
int local_col = item.get_local_id(1);
int global_row = item.get_group(0) * TILE_SIZE + local_row;
int global_col = item.get_group(1) * TILE_SIZE + local_col;

// Collaborative load: each work-item loads exactly one element
tile[local_row][local_col] = global_input[global_row * N + global_col];

// CRITICAL: Synchronize before ANY reads from the tile
sycl::group_barrier(item.get_group());

// All work-items can now read the entire tile from fast SLM
for (int k = 0; k < TILE_SIZE; ++k) {
    sum += tile[local_row][k] * other_tile[k][local_col];
}

// CRITICAL: Synchronize before overwriting the tile
sycl::group_barrier(item.get_group());
```

**2. Select Appropriate Tile Sizes**
- SLM capacity is typically 64KB per work-group
- For `float`: 16×16 tile = 1KB, 32×32 tile = 4KB
- Leave headroom for other local variables

**3. Avoid Bank Conflicts with Padding**
When work-items in the same sub-group access the same column, add padding:

```cpp
// Without padding: bank conflicts when accessing columns
float[TILE_SIZE][TILE_SIZE];          // Conflicts!

// With padding: conflict-free column access
float[TILE_SIZE][TILE_SIZE + 1];      // +1 padding eliminates conflicts
```

### Constraints
- Always call `sycl::group_barrier(item.get_group())` after writes and before reads
- SLM is shared within a work-group; do NOT assume data persists across work-groups
- Handle boundary conditions when tile extends beyond input dimensions
- **CRITICAL: SYCL dimension limit**: `sycl::local_accessor<T, N>` and `sycl::range<N>` require N ∈ {1, 2, 3}. 
  For 4D+ data (e.g., batch×channel×height×width), flatten dimensions:
  ```cpp
  // WRONG: sycl::local_accessor<float, 4> tile(...)  // COMPILE ERROR!
  // CORRECT: Use 2D/3D tile and linearize extra dimensions
  sycl::local_accessor<float, 2> tile(sycl::range<2>(TILE_H, TILE_W), cgh);
  // Handle batch/channel via outer loops or work-group indexing
  ```

