## Memory Optimization: Coalesced & Vectorized Access (OpenCL)

### Objective
Maximize global memory throughput by coalescing accesses and using vector types where alignment permits.

### Required Transformations

- Use contiguous access patterns across work-items in a work-group/wavefront.
- Prefer vector types for aligned contiguous data: `float2`, `float4`, `int4`.
- Add `restrict`/`const` qualifiers to help compiler alias analysis.

```c
// Coalesced pattern
int gid = get_global_id(0);
out[gid] = in[gid] * 2.0f;

// Vectorized load/store when aligned
int vgid = get_global_id(0);
float4 v = vload4(vgid, in);
vstore4(v * 2.0f, vgid, out);
```

### Constraints
- Only vectorize when data alignment and length are compatible.
- Handle tails with scalar fallback when `N % vector_width != 0`.

