## Memory Optimization: Local Memory Tiling (OpenCL)

### Objective
Reduce global memory traffic by staging reusable tiles in `__local` memory.

### Required Transformations

- Cooperatively load a tile from `__global` to `__local`.
- Synchronize with `barrier(CLK_LOCAL_MEM_FENCE)` before reading tile data.
- Add padding in local tiles to reduce bank conflicts for column-wise access.

```c
__local float tile[TILE_H][TILE_W + 1];
int lx = get_local_id(0), ly = get_local_id(1);
int gx = get_group_id(0) * TILE_W + lx;
int gy = get_group_id(1) * TILE_H + ly;

tile[ly][lx] = in[gy * width + gx];
barrier(CLK_LOCAL_MEM_FENCE);

float v = tile[ly][lx];
```

### Constraints
- Keep local memory usage below device limits (`CL_DEVICE_LOCAL_MEM_SIZE`).
- Avoid unnecessary barriers; each barrier has a cost.

