## Parallelism Optimization: Work-Group Cooperative Algorithms

### Objective
Replace sequential or atomic-based operations with efficient cooperative algorithms that leverage all work-items within a work-group simultaneously.

### Required Transformations

**1. Tree Reduction (Replace Atomics)**
Atomic operations serialize access; tree reductions are O(log N) parallel steps:

```cpp
constexpr int WG_SIZE = 256;  // Must be power of 2 for clean reduction

// Allocate local memory for the work-group
auto local_data = sycl::ext::oneapi::group_local_memory_for_overwrite<float[WG_SIZE]>(item.get_group());

int tid = item.get_local_id(0);
int block_id = item.get_group(0);

// Step 1: Each work-item stores its value
local_data[tid] = my_value;
sycl::group_barrier(item.get_group());  // REQUIRED before any reads

// Step 2: Tree reduction - log2(WG_SIZE) iterations
for (int stride = WG_SIZE / 2; stride > 0; stride /= 2) {
    if (tid < stride) {
        local_data[tid] += local_data[tid + stride];
    }
    sycl::group_barrier(item.get_group());  // REQUIRED each iteration
}

// Step 3: Work-item 0 has the final result
if (tid == 0) {
    output[block_id] = local_data[0];
}
```

**2. Synchronization Rules**
| Operation | Barrier Required? |
|-----------|------------------|
| After writing to local memory | YES - `sycl::group_barrier(item.get_group())` |
| Before reading local memory written by others | YES |
| Between reduction iterations | YES |
| After reading (before next write) | YES |

**3. Work-Group Size Selection**
- Must be ≤ device maximum (query `info::device::max_work_group_size`)
- Should be multiple of sub-group size (32 on Intel, 32/64 on AMD/NVIDIA)
- Common choices: 64, 128, 256, 512
- Larger = more parallelism within group; smaller = more groups (better occupancy)

### Constraints
- Tree reduction requires work-group size to be power of 2 (or handle non-power-of-2 with masking)
- Never skip barriers - undefined behavior (data races)
- Local memory is shared only within the work-group, not across work-groups

