## Intel ESIMD (Explicit SIMD) - Complete API Reference

### Critical Notice
ESIMD kernels use a **completely different API** from standard SYCL. Standard SYCL constructs will NOT compile in ESIMD kernels. Follow this reference exactly.

---

### 1. Required Setup

Every ESIMD kernel must include these elements:

```cpp
#include <sycl/ext/intel/esimd.hpp>
using namespace sycl::ext::intel::esimd;

// The kernel MUST have the [[intel::sycl_explicit_simd]] attribute
q.parallel_for(sycl::range<1>(num_work_items), [=](sycl::id<1> idx) [[intel::sycl_explicit_simd]] {
    // ESIMD code only - no standard SYCL work-group functions
});
```

---

### 2. Data Types: `simd<T, N>` is Mandatory

ALL data operations must use `simd<T, N>` vector types. Scalar operations defeat the purpose of ESIMD.

```cpp
constexpr int VL = 16;  // Vector length - typically 8, 16, or 32

// CORRECT: Vector types and operations
simd<float, VL> a = block_load<float, VL>(input + offset);
simd<float, VL> b = block_load<float, VL>(input2 + offset);
simd<float, VL> c = a + b;           // Element-wise vector addition
simd<float, VL> d = a * b;           // Element-wise vector multiplication
simd<float, VL> e = sycl::exp(a);    // Element-wise math functions
block_store(output + offset, c);

// INCORRECT: Scalar operations (DO NOT USE)
float val = input[i];                 // Scalar load - defeats ESIMD
output[i] = val * 2.0f;               // Scalar store - defeats ESIMD
```

---

### 3. Memory Operations

| Operation | ESIMD Syntax | Notes |
|-----------|-------------|-------|
| Aligned vector load | `simd<T,N> v = block_load<T,N>(ptr)` | Pointer must be aligned to N×sizeof(T) |
| Unaligned vector load | `simd<T,N> v = block_load<T,N,N>(ptr, overaligned_tag<1>{})` | For unaligned access |
| Aligned vector store | `block_store(ptr, v)` | Pointer must be aligned |
| Gather (indexed) | `simd<T,N> v = gather<T,N>(ptr, offsets)` | `offsets` is `simd<uint32_t,N>` of byte offsets |
| Scatter (indexed) | `scatter(ptr, offsets, v)` | Indexed store |

```cpp
// Contiguous aligned load/store (most efficient)
constexpr int VL = 16;
int offset = idx * VL;
simd<float, VL> data = block_load<float, VL>(input + offset);
block_store(output + offset, data);

// Gather with arbitrary indices
simd<uint32_t, VL> byte_offsets = /* compute offsets */;
simd<float, VL> gathered = gather<float, VL>(base_ptr, byte_offsets);
```

---

### 4. Shared Local Memory (SLM) in ESIMD

SLM must be initialized with `slm_init<BYTES>()` and accessed with dedicated functions:

```cpp
// Initialize SLM (call once at kernel start)
slm_init<4096>();  // 4096 bytes of SLM

// Write to SLM (byte offset, vector data)
simd<float, 16> data = block_load<float, 16>(global_ptr);
slm_block_store<float, 16>(0, data);              // Store at byte offset 0
slm_block_store<float, 16>(64, other_data);       // Store at byte offset 64

// Synchronize before reading
barrier();  // ESIMD barrier (no arguments)

// Read from SLM
simd<float, 16> loaded = slm_block_load<float, 16>(0);
```

**FORBIDDEN in ESIMD** (use ESIMD equivalents above):
- ❌ `sycl::ext::oneapi::group_local_memory_for_overwrite` 
- ❌ `sycl::group_barrier(item.get_group())`

---

### 5. Reductions in ESIMD

Use the `reduce` function for vector reductions:

```cpp
simd<float, 16> values = block_load<float, 16>(ptr);

// Reduce to scalar
float sum = reduce<float>(values, std::plus<>());
float max_val = reduce<float>(values, std::maximum<>());
float min_val = reduce<float>(values, std::minimum<>());

// Horizontal operations
float product = reduce<float>(values, std::multiplies<>());
```

**FORBIDDEN in ESIMD**:
- ❌ `sycl::reduce_over_group(sg, value, op)`

---

### 6. Atomic Operations in ESIMD

Use `atomic_update` with explicit atomic operation type:

```cpp
simd<float, 16> values_to_add = /* ... */;

// Atomic add to global memory
atomic_update<atomic_op::fadd>(global_ptr + offset, values_to_add);

// Atomic operations available:
// atomic_op::add, atomic_op::sub, atomic_op::inc, atomic_op::dec
// atomic_op::min, atomic_op::max
// atomic_op::fadd, atomic_op::fsub (for floats)
// atomic_op::cmpxchg, atomic_op::xchg
// atomic_op::bit_and, atomic_op::bit_or, atomic_op::bit_xor
```

**FORBIDDEN in ESIMD**:
- ❌ `sycl::atomic_ref<T, ...>(ptr).fetch_add(value)`

---

### 7. Barriers and Synchronization

```cpp
// ESIMD barrier (synchronizes all work-items that share SLM)
barrier();  // No arguments!

// Memory fence
fence<memory_kind::global>();   // Global memory fence
fence<memory_kind::local>();    // Local/SLM memory fence
```

**FORBIDDEN in ESIMD**:
- ❌ `sycl::group_barrier(item.get_group())`
- ❌ `item.barrier()`

---

### 8. Complete ESIMD Kernel Example

```cpp
#include <sycl/sycl.hpp>
#include <sycl/ext/intel/esimd.hpp>
using namespace sycl::ext::intel::esimd;

constexpr int VL = 16;
constexpr int SLM_SIZE = 4096;

q.parallel_for(sycl::range<1>(N / VL), [=](sycl::id<1> idx) [[intel::sycl_explicit_simd]] {
    slm_init<SLM_SIZE>();

    int offset = idx * VL;

    // Load from global memory
    simd<float, VL> a = block_load<float, VL>(input_a + offset);
    simd<float, VL> b = block_load<float, VL>(input_b + offset);

    // Compute
    simd<float, VL> c = a + b;
    simd<float, VL> d = sycl::exp(c);

    // Store to SLM for sharing
    slm_block_store<float, VL>(0, d);
    barrier();

    // Load back (in real code, different work-items would read each other's data)
    simd<float, VL> from_slm = slm_block_load<float, VL>(0);

    // Reduce and store
    float local_sum = reduce<float>(from_slm, std::plus<>());
    if (idx == 0) {
        atomic_update<atomic_op::fadd>(output, simd<float, 1>(local_sum));
    }
});
```

---

### Common Mistakes to Avoid

| Mistake | Consequence | Correction |
|---------|-------------|------------|
| Using scalar types | Performance loss, defeats ESIMD | Always use `simd<T,N>` |
| Using `group_local_memory_for_overwrite` | Compilation error | Use `slm_init` + `slm_block_load/store` |
| Using `reduce_over_group` | Compilation error | Use `reduce<T>(simd_val, op)` |
| Using `sycl::group_barrier` | Compilation error | Use `barrier()` |
| Mixing ESIMD and standard SYCL | Compilation error | Keep kernels pure ESIMD |

